{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"shared product vision shared product vision","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md","fileName":"Shared Product Vision.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Shared Product Vision","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Production Planning and Milestones]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Production Planning and Milestones","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"shared product vision shared product vision","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Shared Product Vision.md","fileName":"Shared Product Vision.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Shared Product Vision","heading":"Shared Product Vision","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A shared product vision is a clear, compelling, and stable understanding of what a team is making, what it will deliver, and how each person's work contributes. It turns a creative direction into coordinated action.\n\nThe vision should be documented, understood, and supported across the team without becoming immune to evidence. Necessary changes involve relevant stakeholders and are communicated deliberately so the project does not drift through accumulated local decisions.\n\nRelease planning can revisit the vision through a concise elevator statement, game-box exercise, positioning map, or ambitious release goal. The representation matters less than giving developers enough shared context to make aligned daily decisions while features emerge.","tags":["baby"],"li